# an untyped shift is exact, so its value is checked where it lands: 2^63 is
# past i64, which `a` binds -- it was i64's minimum, silently -- and a shift
# past the 512 bits an untyped integer holds overflows wherever it is written,
# even before `>>` would bring it back.
main: function is {
    a: 1 << 63
    b: (1 << 600) >> 590
    print "\{a} \{b}"
}
